            <ArticleTitle>Ergotamine-induced headache can be sustained by sumatriptan daily intake.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>374-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We describe the case report of a migraine sufferer who developed ergotamine-induced headache and subsequently replaced ergotamine with daily sumatriptan (100 mg p.o.). The features of the headache were unchanged except for the presence of superimposed migraine-like headaches that occurred every 24 h.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
